    "notes": "The real typecheck (cd books && npx tsc -p . | grep procedures.ts) shows only \"Cannot find module './neighbors.ts'\": neighbors.ts did not exist yet, while foundation.ts, vocabulary.ts and data.ts did. To check the rest, I copied procedures.ts, data.ts, foundation.ts and vocabulary.ts into the scratchpad (/tmp/claude-0/-home-user/c92cd756-b1a0-5414-9fe4-a7834db8d32a/scratchpad/tc) with a stub neighbors.ts that uses the conventional names. tsc reported no errors there, and a runtime import passed the decode checks of all 65 records with no duplicate ids or links. My neighbour names match what commands.ts, executions.ts, schedules.ts and verifications.ts import.\n\nScope: the 60 *InTx exports on the door, plus 5 non-suffixed exports that take the caller's ctx: lookupActorRecipient, lookupPartyRecipient, lookupPaymentRecipient, actorInventory, explainedByCapxul. Not booked as procedures: pure rules, Effect and ActionCtx helpers (buildOrReuseExecution, storeBuiltExecution, submitStoredExecution, recoverSubmissionClaim, checkoutPrepared, ownersScheduledExecution, ownersVoidExecution, plannedOwners, the budget and roles-module checks, scheduledSubmitted) and pure functions (readPaymentReplayIntent, isAcceptedPaymentReplay, expectedFactsForItem, ...).\n\nHow records are built: reads and writes are transitive within payments (view, authority and recipient helpers). A neighbour function is an invokes. Birth transitions follow data.ts, which models a birth as to_pending or to_scheduled etc. I removed payment_transitioned from apply-payout-rail-delivery's emits, because its transitions already carry it. Each about names today's callers with file and line, from a grep of #payments/... subpath imports; no concept imports the door file \"#payments\" itself.\n\nFindings recorded as they are:\n- Neighbour tables read directly: accounts, identities, orgs, counterpartyDestinations, financialDocumentLinks, paymentRequests.\n- Neighbour table written directly: invoiceCheckoutPayments, by prepare-payment-command.\n- ensure-proof-payout inserts an in_transit Payment outside the sole writer.\n- No other concept invokes readOutsideMoneyOrgsInTx, serverPaymentAuthorityInTx or loadPaymentRetrySourceInTx today.\n\nNot representable in the schema, so written in about instead:\n- The scheduled workflows payments.verifications.settle and payments.verifications.verify.\n- The caller callbacks onAuthorized, onLifecyclePayment and observation.onAuthorized.\n- capture-memo-conflict-removal returns a function the caller runs later in the same transaction."
